{"id":"mahabharata-3-202","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":202,"title":"द्व्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 202 · Mind and the self","summary":{"en":"At Kaushika's request the hunter speaks further of the mind: how one who controls it sees the self pervading the world and the world in the self. He describes the qualities that bewilder men when the fruits of action come, and the steadfast meditation that overcomes them.","kn":"ಕೌಶಿಕನ ಕೋರಿಕೆಯಂತೆ ವ್ಯಾಧನು ಮನಸ್ಸಿನ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಮತ್ತಷ್ಟು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ: ಅದನ್ನು ನಿಗ್ರಹಿಸಿದವನು ಲೋಕದಲ್ಲಿ ಆತ್ಮವನ್ನೂ ಆತ್ಮದಲ್ಲಿ ಲೋಕವನ್ನೂ ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕರ್ಮಫಲ ಬಂದಾಗ ಮನುಷ್ಯರನ್ನು ಮೋಹಗೊಳಿಸುವ ಗುಣಗಳನ್ನೂ ಅವುಗಳನ್ನು ಗೆಲ್ಲುವ ಸ್ಥಿರ ಧ್ಯಾನವನ್ನೂ ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कौशिक के अनुरोध पर व्याध मन के विषय में और बताता है: जो उसे वश में करता है वह संसार में आत्मा को और आत्मा में संसार को देखता है। वह उन गुणों का वर्णन करता है जो कर्मफल आने पर मनुष्यों को मोहित करते हैं, और उन्हें जीतने वाले स्थिर ध्यान का।","te":"కౌశికుని కోరికపై వ్యాధుడు మనస్సు గురించి మరింత చెబుతాడు: దానిని నిగ్రహించినవాడు లోకంలో ఆత్మను, ఆత్మలో లోకాన్ని చూస్తాడు. కర్మఫలం వచ్చినప్పుడు మనుషులను మోహింపజేసే గుణాలను, వాటిని జయించే స్థిర ధ్యానాన్ని వర్ణిస్తాడు.","ta":"கௌஶிகரின் வேண்டுகோளின்படி வ்யாதன் மனத்தைப் பற்றி மேலும் சொல்கிறான்: அதை அடக்கியவன் உலகில் ஆன்மாவையும் ஆன்மாவில் உலகையும் காண்கிறான். வினைப்பயன் வரும்போது மனிதரை மயக்கும் குணங்களையும் அவற்றை வெல்லும் உறுதியான தியானத்தையும் விவரிக்கிறான்.","ml":"കൗശികന്റെ അഭ്യർത്ഥനപ്രകാരം വ്യാധൻ മനസ്സിനെക്കുറിച്ച് കൂടുതൽ പറയുന്നു: അത് നിയന്ത്രിക്കുന്നവൻ, ലോകത്ത് വ്യാപിച്ച ആത്മാവിനെയും ആത്മാവിൽ ലോകത്തെയും കാണുന്നു. കർമ്മഫലം വരുമ്പോൾ മനുഷ്യരെ മോഹിപ്പിക്കുന്ന ഗുണങ്ങളെയും, അവയെ മറികടക്കുന്ന ഉറച്ച ധ്യാനത്തെയും അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.202; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमुक्तः स विप्रस्तु धर्मव्याधेन भारत ।\nकथामकथयद्भूयो मनसः प्रीतिवर्धनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Addressed thus by the dharma-hunter, Bharata, the brahmin spoke further, in talk that increased the mind's delight."}},{"text":"ब्राह्मण","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"महाभूतानि यान्याहुः पञ्च धर्मविदां वर ।\nएकैकस्य गुणान्सम्यक्पञ्चानामपि मे वद ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of those who know dharma, tell me rightly the qualities of each of the five great elements that are spoken of."}},{"text":"व्याध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"भूमिरापस्तथा ज्योतिर्वायुराकाशमेव च ।\nगुणोत्तराणि सर्वाणि तेषां वक्ष्यामि ते गुणान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Earth, water, fire, wind and space: each one has more qualities than the one before. I will tell you their qualities."}},{"n":4,"text":"भूमिः पञ्चगुणा ब्रह्मन्नुदकं च चतुर्गुणम् ।\nगुणास्त्रयस्तेजसि च त्रयश्चाकाशवातयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Earth has five qualities, brahmin, water four, and fire has three, and space and wind two each."}},{"n":5,"text":"शब्दः स्पर्शश्च रूपं च रसो गन्धश्च पञ्चमः ।\nएते गुणाः पञ्च भूमेः सर्वेभ्यो गुणवत्तराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sound, touch, form, taste and, fifth, smell are the five qualities of earth, which has more qualities than all."}},{"n":6,"text":"शब्दः स्पर्शश्च रूपं च रसश्चापि द्विजोत्तम ।\nअपामेते गुणा ब्रह्मन्कीर्तितास्तव सुव्रत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sound, touch, form and also taste, best of brahmins, these are the qualities of water, brahmin, that I have told you, of good vows."}},{"n":7,"text":"शब्दः स्पर्शश्च रूपं च तेजसोऽथ गुणास्त्रयः ।\nशब्दः स्पर्शश्च वायौ तु शब्द आकाश एव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sound, touch and form are the three qualities of fire; in wind there are sound and touch, and in space, sound alone."}},{"n":8,"text":"एते पञ्चदश ब्रह्मन्गुणा भूतेषु पञ्चसु ।\nवर्तन्ते सर्वभूतेषु येषु लोकाः प्रतिष्ठिताः ।\nअन्योन्यं नातिवर्तन्ते संपच्च भवति द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"These fifteen qualities, brahmin, abide in the five elements, in all beings in which the worlds are established; they do not overstep one another, and so there is prosperity, brahmin."}},{"n":9,"text":"यदा तु विषमीभावमाचरन्ति चराचराः ।\nतदा देही देहमन्यं व्यतिरोहति कालतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But when moving and unmoving beings fall into disharmony, then the embodied self, with time, leaves the body for another."}},{"n":10,"text":"आनुपूर्व्या विनश्यन्ति जायन्ते चानुपूर्वशः ।\nतत्र तत्र हि दृश्यन्ते धातवः पाञ्चभौतिकाः ।\nयैरावृतमिदं सर्वं जगत्स्थावरजङ्गमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They perish in order and are born in order; in each place the five-element substances are seen, by which all this world, moving and unmoving, is covered."}},{"n":11,"text":"इन्द्रियैः सृज्यते यद्यत्तत्तद्व्यक्तमिति स्मृतम् ।\nअव्यक्तमिति विज्ञेयं लिङ्गग्राह्यमतीन्द्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever is produced by the senses is remembered as manifest; the unmanifest is to be understood as what is grasped by inference and lies beyond the senses."}},{"n":12,"text":"यथास्वं ग्राहकान्येषां शब्दादीनामिमानि तु ।\nइन्द्रियाणि यदा देही धारयन्निह तप्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"These senses, each grasping its own objects such as sound, are what the embodied self holds in check here, and it is pained."}},{"n":13,"text":"लोके विततमात्मानं लोकं चात्मनि पश्यति ।\nपरावरज्ञः सक्तः सन्सर्वभूतानि पश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He sees the self spread through the world and the world in the self; knowing the higher and lower, though attached, he sees all beings."}},{"n":14,"text":"पश्यतः सर्वभूतानि सर्वावस्थासु सर्वदा ।\nब्रह्मभूतस्य संयोगो नाशुभेनोपपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who sees all beings in all states at all times, who has become Brahman, no connection with evil arises."}},{"n":15,"text":"ज्ञानमूलात्मकं क्लेशमतिवृत्तस्य मोहजम् ।\nलोको बुद्धिप्रकाशेन ज्ञेयमार्गेण दृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who has passed beyond affliction born of delusion, rooted in knowledge, the world is seen by the light of understanding along the path of what is to be known."}},{"n":16,"text":"अनादिनिधनं जन्तुमात्मयोनिं सदाव्ययम् ।\nअनौपम्यममूर्तं च भगवानाह बुद्धिमान् ।\nतपोमूलमिदं सर्वं यन्मां विप्रानुपृच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blessed wise one speaks of the creature without beginning or end, self-born and ever imperishable, without likeness and without form; all this that you ask me about, brahmin, has austerity as its root."}},{"n":17,"text":"इन्द्रियाण्येव तत्सर्वं यत्स्वर्गनरकावुभौ ।\nनिगृहीतविसृष्टानि स्वर्गाय नरकाय च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The senses are all that: both heaven and hell. Restrained or let loose, they lead to heaven or to hell."}},{"n":18,"text":"एष योगविधिः कृत्स्नो यावदिन्द्रियधारणम् ।\nएतन्मूलं हि तपसः कृत्स्नस्य नरकस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the whole rule of yoga, as far as holding the senses goes; this is the root of all austerity and also of hell."}},{"n":19,"text":"इन्द्रियाणां प्रसङ्गेन दोषमृच्छत्यसंशयम् ।\nसंनियम्य तु तान्येव ततः सिद्धिमवाप्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"By indulgence in the senses a man undoubtedly incurs fault; by restraining them he attains perfection."}},{"n":20,"text":"षण्णामात्मनि नित्यानामैश्वर्यं योऽधिगच्छति ।\nन स पापैः कुतोऽनर्थैर्युज्यते विजितेन्द्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gains lordship over the six that dwell eternally in the self, a man of conquered senses, how could he be joined to sins and ruin?"}},{"n":21,"text":"रथः शरीरं पुरुषस्य दृष्ट-\nमात्मा नियन्तेन्द्रियाण्याहुरश्वान् ।\nतैरप्रमत्तः कुशली सदश्वै-\nर्दान्तैः सुखं याति रथीव धीरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The body of a man is seen as a chariot, the self the driver, and the senses are called the horses; the wise, skilful man, unheedless with those good, tamed horses, goes happily like a charioteer."}},{"n":22,"text":"षण्णामात्मनि नित्यानामिन्द्रियाणां प्रमाथिनाम् ।\nयो धीरो धारयेद्रश्मीन्स स्यात्परमसारथिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of the six, the senses that dwell eternally in the self and are agitating, the steady man who holds the reins would be the best charioteer."}},{"n":23,"text":"इन्द्रियाणां प्रसृष्टानां हयानामिव वर्त्मसु ।\nधृतिं कुर्वीत सारथ्ये धृत्या तानि जयेद्ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For senses let loose like horses on the roads, one should make steadiness in the driving, and by steadiness conquer them surely."}},{"n":24,"text":"इन्द्रियाणां हि चरतां यन्मनोऽनुविधीयते ।\nतदस्य हरते बुद्धिं नावं वायुरिवाम्भसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whichever of the roaming senses the mind follows, it carries away his understanding, as wind carries a boat on water."}},{"n":25,"text":"येषु विप्रतिपद्यन्ते षट्सु मोहात्फलागमे ।\nतेष्वध्यवसिताध्यायी विन्दते ध्यानजं फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In these six, where through delusion people contend when a result comes, one who has fixed his meditation upon them finds the fruit born of meditation."}}]}]}